In article <1991Feb19.083822.19029@portia.Stanford.EDU>, toddc@portia.Stanford.EDU (Todd C. Merrill) writes:
> What does the attribute HD mean?  Specifically, I noticed that when fooling 
> around in explore mode, I polymorphed myself into a monster, and the attribute
> that is Xp for humans turned into HD when I was the monster.  Apparently, it
> is some measure of the experience of the monster, but what do the letters 'HD'
> stand for?

Again Hack's roots in (A)D&D show up. Hit Dice are used to determine how many
hit points a creature has, and therefore a reliable guide to the monster's
toughness.

